This also lets us build “encounter grammars”

Meaning we can classify matchups by structure:

* brute force vs agility
* armor vs penetration
* ambush vs endurance
* reach vs mobility
* single heavy striker vs distributed limb control
* venom/time-delay kill vs immediate trauma kill

Then a cave bear vs giant spider becomes one expression of a deeper pattern.

That means we can compare it to:

* bear vs big cat
* knight vs giant octopus
* boar vs tiger
* armored vehicle vs drone swarm
* wrestler vs knife fighter

Different substrate, same structural grammar.

That’s very Pantheon.

